      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Multi Stitch Images — a grid from several IMAGE inputs\n\nThree Load Image nodes (ComfyUI's bundled example.png) go straight into images, images_2 and images_3. Plugging one in opens the next socket, so there is always a spare; each input keeps its own size, exactly like an image pasted onto the node, and no Batch Images is needed to join them.\n\nThe node lays them out as a 2-column grid with an 8 px black gap, caps the long side at 1024 px, and output_cells fills the cells output with each picture centred in a uniform cell.\n\nImages pasted onto the node come first; the input pictures follow in socket order. Replace example.png with your own files, or feed a socket from any node that outputs an image or a batch."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
